    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n101027" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συντῑμ-άω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>honour together</i> or <i>alike</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				31.31
			</span></i> (
				Pass.
			); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span>
			<i>with</i> another, Apollod.Hist.<i><span class="en">
				147
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i> (
				Pass.
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Med.
			, <i>value</i> or <i>estimate</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συνετιμήσανθ᾽ ὑπὲρ ἐμοῦ ταύτην τὴν
				εἰσφοράν</span>
			<i>they fixed</i> this <i>as the estimate of</i> my
			contribution, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				27.8
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				28.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PPetr.</u>
				2p.83
			</span></i>, al. <span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, etc.:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅθεν περ . . συνετιμήθη τὰ
				περὶ τὸν σῖτον</span> and that is how <i>prices were
				rigged</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				56.8
			</span></i>.</div>
